post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'
tar1090 is a web page on top of an existing decoder; nothing runs until you:
  1. Set SOURCE_DIR in /etc/default/tar1090 to where your decoder writes aircraft.json
     (readsb-git: /run/readsb, dump1090-fa-git: /run/dump1090) and match it in the
     web server snippet.
  2. lighttpd: add to /etc/lighttpd/lighttpd.conf
       server.modules += ("mod_alias", "mod_redirect", "mod_setenv")
       include "conf.d/tar1090.conf"
     nginx: include /usr/share/doc/tar1090/nginx-tar1090.conf in your server {} block.
  3. systemctl enable --now tar1090   (track history; the map works without it)
Web interface: http://<host>/tar1090/
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    systemctl try-restart tar1090.service 2>/dev/null || true
}
